/*!
@defgroup resetcon RESETCON Driver
@details The MCUXpresso SDK provides APIs for MCUXpresso SDK devices' Reset Controller operation.

The Reset Controller (RESETCON) collates the different reset sources of the chip,
generates the global reset for all power domains, and records the source of the
latest and previous reset events.

The RESETCON driver supports:
  - Configuring access control (domain mask, user-mode, non-secure mode, lock)
  - Triggering a global software warm reset via the SWRST magic value
  - Reading and clearing latched and sticky reset-source status (RSTSTAT, RSTSTAT_STICKY)
  - Reading and clearing per-power-domain reset status (PD_RSTSTAT, PD_RSTSTAT_STICKY)
  - Triggering software-controlled NPU / Media / Communication power-domain resets
  - Enabling warm-to-cold reset escalation per source (ESCAEN, sticky until cold reset)
  - Routing warm-reset sources to interrupts with configurable timeout (RSTIE, RSTIS, ITO)
  - Masking individual warm-reset sources and selecting level vs. edge trigger mode
  - Configuring RESET_b and POR_b digital filters and enabling POR-triggered PMU restart
  - Reading the latched boot-mode pins and overriding the boot mode for the next warm reset
  - Reading and clearing the warm-reset count
  - Reading and writing the 16-entry general-purpose retention register array, with per-entry locks

*/
